---
description: Cursor rules for Git development with conventional commit messages integration.
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: false
---
Use the Conventional Commit Messages specification to generate commit messages

The commit message should be structured as follows:

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

The commit contains the following structural elements, to communicate intent:

- `fix`: patches a bug (PATCH in SemVer)
- `feat`: introduces a new feature (MINOR in SemVer)
- `BREAKING CHANGE`: footer, or `!` after type/scope (MAJOR in SemVer)
- Other types: `build`, `chore`, `ci`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`

A scope MAY be provided after a type, e.g. `feat(wasm):`.

A description MUST immediately follow the colon and space after the type/scope prefix.

A longer commit body MAY be provided after one blank line.

Breaking changes MUST be indicated with `!` before `:` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
